config CORDIC
	tristate "CORDIC algorithm"
	help
	  This option provides an implementation of the CORDIC algorithm;
	  calculations are in fixed point. Module will be called cordic.

config PRIME_NUMBERS
	tristate "Simple prime number generator for testing"
	help
	  This option provides a simple prime number generator for test
	  modules.

	  If unsure, say N.

config RATIONAL
	tristate "rational_best_approximation() function"
	help
	  Provides rational_best_approximation(), which finds the best
	  rational approximation of a fraction within given numerator and
	  denominator limits. Drivers that need it select it.

	  RUSTY-LINUX DIVERGENCE: upstream has no prompt here, so the
	  symbol is select-only and CONFIG_RATIONAL=y in a fragment is
	  silently discarded by olddefconfig -- the same shape as
	  CONFIG_GLOB, and caught the same way, by rig/config.sh reading
	  the built .config back. config-fast needs it so the ported
	  function is exercised on the iteration instrument too. No
	  existing config changes: every in-tree user still selects it.

	  Say N unless you are working on the Rust port.

config MATH_SELFTEST
	tristate "lib/math self-test on init"
	help
	  A handful of vectors for the lib/math functions that have been
	  ported to Rust, run from an initcall. It prints
	  "mathtest: N self-tests passed, M failed" and refuses to load if
	  any failed.

	  It is not a correctness suite -- that lives in userspace and runs
	  tens of millions of cases. This answers the one question a
	  userspace test cannot: whether the Rust ran, in the kernel.

	  Say N unless you are working on the Rust port.
